{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792164660,"nonce":"cbOLCVU/nQrWL74QkWy9Wlnupsw=","title":"Structural field access assumed the structure's own layout","message":"A value typed as a structure (`typedef View = {text:String, ...}`) was read and written by the structure's name-sorted field index. That is only right for an anonymous object built in that layout: a class instance passed where the structure is expected crashed, and a wider anonymous object read the wrong slot or lost writes.\n\nFix: `rayzor_anon_get_struct_field` / `rayzor_anon_set_struct_field` take the index, the structure's shape id and the field name. A matching shape reads by index; any other anonymous object is searched by name; a class instance goes through its field registry, converting `Null\u003cInt\u003e` between the class's unboxed slot and the structure's boxed one. wasm delegates to the by-index functions (its objects are always anonymous).\n\nRegression: haxe-conformance/regressions/StructuralStorage.hx.\n\nThis is what lets the typer accept a class instance where a structure is expected (TestType unification).","files":null}]}